# CP5 W4 — a creature blocks the step, and a killed one does not.
#
# Run against a data dir whose monx31 places slot0 at (1,0) with hp 25, and a
# save whose entry position is (0,0). The patch is two bytes in monx31:
#   file[0]=1, file[32]=0, file[64]=25, file[96]=0x68
# (x, y, hp, type for slot 0 — see docs/monster-spawn.md § 2 for the layout.)
#
# Expected CMD window, in order:
#   CMD: ATTACK--EAST--HIT!!!
#   CMD: KILLED--GOLD+3--EXP.+04
#   CMD: EAST
# The third line is the point: the step is accepted only because the creature in
# it is dead. With the creature alive, EAST prints `EAST--INVALID MOVE!` and the
# player stays put; NORTH, where nothing stands, prints a bare `NORTH`.
#
# NOT A GATE. This sequence was run by hand on 2026-10-23 and is recorded so the
# next agent re-runs it rather than re-deriving it. Nothing in `make test`
# executes it yet — see docs/phase4-state.md CP5 W4.
A
0xf3
0xf3
